msh — My Parallel SSH

Usage:
  msh <command> [flags]
  msh --help
  msh --version

Commands:
  c             Short form of task run: msh c TASK SERVER
  config        Show and validate configuration
  exec          Run a command on servers
  help          Show help for msh or for one command
  hosts         List and check inventory servers
  logs          Show or follow a log file on servers
  script        Run a local script on servers without copying it
  shell         Open an interactive shell on a server
  task          List, show and run configured tasks
  version       Print version information

Shortcuts (read-only, same selection flags as exec):
  ping          Check SSH connectivity and authentication
  uname         Show system information (uname -a)
  kernel        Show the kernel release (uname -r)
  uptime        Show uptime and load averages
  disk          Show filesystem usage (df -hP)
  memory        Show memory usage in MiB (free -m)
  services      List running systemd services
  failed-units  List failed systemd units
  selinux       Show the SELinux mode (getenforce)

Run 'msh help <command>' for details about a command.
